#
# ⑤ ⭐⭐ A DOOR RE-CONFIRMS IT HOLDS THE BOX IN THE SAME BREATH AS STARTING ANYTHING THAT PUTS A
#    BEAM ON IT — not at grant time, not at take time, but IMMEDIATELY BEFORE THE RUN.
#    ⛔ RULED 2026-09-03T16:58Z from next's own diagnosis after it ran BUMP-LOG-1's gate block while
#      the grant was chit's: "RELEASING IS AN EVENT AND HOLDING IS A STATE, AND I ONLY EVER
#      REPRESENTED THE EVENT." It sent "RELEASING NOW" and nothing changed afterwards — no expiry to
#      trip, no check before starting a suite, nothing that would have said "you are not holding it".
#    ⭐ ITS OWN PARALLEL, which is why this is a PRECONDITION and not an etiquette: ①–④ are
#      re-verified immediately before a push rather than at warrant time, because A WARRANT IS ISSUED
#      AGAINST A STATE AND THE PUSH HAPPENS AGAINST A LATER ONE. next acted on a fact that HAD BEEN
#      TRUE — the identical defect at a different door.
#    ⚠️ AND IT INDICTS THIS PROTOCOL MORE THAN THE DOOR: next's own box check runs WHEN IT TAKES the
#      box and never WHEN IT STARTS A RUN, so from inside "I hold it" and "I held it twenty minutes
#      ago" are indistinguishable. v2 gave it no way to ask the question at the moment it mattered.
#
# ③ ⛔ THE FALLBACK IS NOT A LICENCE TO SKIP ASKING. It exists for MY absence, not for impatience.
#    A door that has had a reply from me inside 30 minutes has an arbiter and must use it.
#
# ⚠️ NOT PROVEN. This has never run. Its first live firing will meet exactly the ambiguity biscuit
#   found in the heartbeat — a door measuring "free" cannot see another door about to start, which is
#   why (c) and (d) exist and why they are the parts most likely to be wrong.

